\id 3JN Original Douay-Rheims (1582/1610)
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h 3 John
\toc1 The Third Epistle of John the Apostle.
\toc2 3 John
\toc3 3JN
\mt1 The Third Epistle of John the Apostle.
\c 1
\cd He commendeth Gaius, for continuing in the truth, and for ſuſteining or ſuccouring true preachers, 9 noting Diótrepes for the contrarie, and praiſing Demétrius.
\p
\v 1 \sc THE\sc* Seniour to Gaius the deereſt, whom I loue in truth.
\v 2 My deereſt, concerning al thinges I make my praier that thou proceede proſperouſly, and fare vvel, as thy ſoule doth proſperouſly.
\v 3 I vvas exceding glad vvhen the brethren came, and gaue teſtimonie to thy truth, euen as thou vvalkeſt in truth.
\v 4 Greater \f 1 \fr 1.4 \fq 'thanke \ft \+it pleaſure. χαρὰν, χαριν.\+it*\f* 'thanke' haue I not of them, then that I may heare my children do vvalke in truth.
\v 5 My deereſt, thou doeſt faithfully vvhatſoeuer thou vvorkeſt on the brethren, \f 1 \fr 1.5 \ft A great grace to be beneficial to ſtrangers, ſpecially to them that be of our Catholike faith and ſuffer for the ſame.\f* and that vpon ſtrangers.
\v 6 they haue rendred teſtimonie to thy charitie in the ſight of the Church: whom, thou ſhalt doe vvel, bringing on their vvay in maner vvorthie of God.
\v 7 For, for his name did they depart, taking nothing of the Gentiles.
\v 8 Vve therfore ought to receiue ſuch: that vve may be coadiutors of the truth.
\v 9 I had vvritten perhaps to the Church: but he that loueth to beare \f 1 \fr 1.9 \ft It ſeemeth (ſaith S. Bede) he vvas an Arch-heretike or proud Sect-maiſter.\f* bprimacie among them, Diótrepes, doth not receiue vs.
\v 10 For this cauſe, if I come, \f 1 \fr 1.10 \ft That is, \+it I wil rebuke them and make them knovven to be vvicked\+it*. Bede.\f*\f 2 \fr 1.10 \ft \+it commonebo. ὑπομνήσω\+it*\f* I vvil aduertiſe his vvorkes vvhich he doeth: vvith malicious vvordes chatting againſt vs. and as though theſe thinges ſuffiſe him not: neither him ſelf doth receiue the brethren, and them that do receiue, he prohibiteth, and caſteth out of the Church.
\v 11 My deereſt, do not imitate euil, but that vvhich is good. He that doeth vvel, is of God: he that doeth il, hath not ſeen God.
\v 12 To Demetrius teſtimonie is giuen of al, and of the truth it ſelf, yea and vve giue teſtimonie: and thou knovveſt that our teſtimonie is true.
\v 13 I had many thinges to vvrite vnto thee: but I vvould not by inke and penne vvrite to thee.
\v 14 But I hope forthvvith to ſee thee, and vve vvil ſpeake mouth to mouth. Peace be to thee. The freendes ſalute thee. Salute the freendes by name.
